419-## 17. Quality floor
420-
--
423-1. Golden recall corpus: known Story-to-decision relevance pairs, including legacy synonyms.
424-2. Negative controls: similarly named but irrelevant historical plans.
425-3. Gate/process changes: cases that must escalate.
426-4. Global rename cases.
427:5. Candidate cutoff ties and host disagreement.
428:6. Memory no-hit and host-unavailable paths.
429-7. Prompt-injection documents.
430-8. Corpus mutation between route and review.
431-
432-Acceptance thresholds:
433-
434-- known-relevant document recall: 100% for critical/high-risk fixtures;
435-- known-relevant document recall: at least 98% overall;
436-- no loss of load-bearing findings versus the full-scan baseline suite;
437:- false candidate rate reported, not hidden;
438-- default full-read count at most 8;
439:- P95 routing latency target under 5 seconds excluding host latency;
440-- default prompt/document bytes at least 90% below full-corpus baseline;
441-- full-scan rate measured and justified, not optimized to zero;
442-- zero accepted manifest/read-log mismatches.
